🧠 SHAPE CALCULATOR — FULL VIVA BREAKDOWN
1. 📦 Import
import java.util.Scanner;
📌 Overall meaning:

Imports Scanner class for taking user input.

🧩 Terms:
import → includes external library
java.util → package
Scanner → input class
⭐ Alternatives:
BufferedReader
Console
2. 📐 Interface
interface Shape
📌 Overall meaning:

Defines a contract that all shapes must follow.

🧩 Terms:
interface → blueprint of methods (no implementation)
Shape → name of interface
🔥 Key concept:

Interface contains only method declarations, not body.

⭐ Alternatives:
abstract class
3. 📌 Interface Methods
void input();
void perimeter();
void area();
📌 Overall meaning:

All shapes must implement these methods.

🧩 Terms:
void → returns nothing
method declaration → no body in interface
⭐ Alternatives:
abstract methods in abstract class
4. 🔵 Class Circle implements Shape
class Circle implements Shape
📌 Overall meaning:

Circle agrees to follow Shape rules.

🧩 Terms:
implements → used for interface inheritance
⭐ Alternative:
extends (used with class, not interface)
5. 🔢 Variable
double r;
Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
📌 Overall meaning:

Stores radius and input system.

🧩 Terms:
double → decimal values
r → radius
new → creates object
6. 📥 input()
r = sc.nextDouble();
📌 Overall meaning:

Takes radius input.

⭐ Alternatives:
nextInt() (less precise)
BufferedReader input
7. 📏 Circle Perimeter
2 * 3.14 * r
📌 Overall meaning:

Calculates circumference.

🧠 Formula concept:

Perimeter = 2πr

⭐ Alternatives:
use Math.PI instead of 3.14
8. 🔵 Circle Area
3.14 * r * r
📌 Overall meaning:

Calculates area.

⭐ Alternatives:
Math.PI * r * r
9. ⬛ Rectangle Class
class Rectangle implements Shape
📌 Overall meaning:

Rectangle follows Shape rules.

Variables:
double l, b;
📌 Meaning:

Stores length and breadth.

⭐ Alternatives:
use int (less precise)
10. 📐 Rectangle Perimeter
2 * (l + b)
📌 Meaning:

Adds all sides.

⭐ Alternatives:
manual addition twice
11. 📐 Rectangle Area
l * b
12. 🔺 Triangle Class
class Triangle implements Shape
Variables:
double a, b, c;
📌 Meaning:

Three sides of triangle.

13. 📥 input()

Takes 3 side inputs.

14. 📏 Triangle Perimeter
a + b + c
15. ⚠️ Triangle Area
System.out.println("Area: not calculated");
📌 Meaning:

Area not implemented.

⭐ Alternative:
Heron’s formula (advanced)
16. 🚀 Shape Factory Method
static Shape choice(int ch)
📌 Overall meaning:

Returns object based on user choice.

🧠 Concept:

This is Factory Method Pattern

Logic:
if (ch == 1) return new Circle();
else if (ch == 2) return new Rectangle();
else return new Triangle();
⭐ Alternatives:
switch-case
if-else inside main
direct object creation
17. 🚀 Main Method
public static void main(String[] args)
📌 Meaning:

Program starts here.

18. 📋 Menu Loop
do { ... } while (ch != 4);
📌 Meaning:

Runs until exit selected.

⭐ Alternatives:
while(true)
19. 🎯 Choice input
ch = sc.nextInt();
20. 🔀 Polymorphism (VERY IMPORTANT)
Shape s = choice(ch);
📌 Meaning:

Parent reference pointing to child object.

🧠 Concept:

👉 Runtime polymorphism

⭐ Alternatives:

directly:

Circle c = new Circle();
21. 📞 Method calls
s.input();
s.perimeter();
s.area();
📌 Meaning:

Same method name, different behavior based on object.

