🟢 1. Interface
contract for classes
🟢 2. Implements
used for interface inheritance
🟢 3. Polymorphism
one reference, many forms
🟢 4. Method Overriding
same methods in different classes
🟢 5. Factory Method
returns objects dynamically
🟢 6. Scanner input
user input handling
🟢 7. Loops
do-while menu system
⚡ CONCEPTUAL VIVA QUESTIONS
❓ What is interface?

👉 A blueprint that defines methods without implementation.

❓ Difference between interface and class?

👉 Class = implementation
👉 Interface = contract

❓ Why use implements?

👉 To inherit interface methods.

❓ What is polymorphism?

👉 One interface, many implementations.

❓ What is runtime polymorphism here?

👉 Shape reference pointing to Circle/Rectangle/Triangle objects.

❓ Why use Shape reference?

👉 To achieve flexibility and dynamic behavior.

❓ What is factory method?

👉 Method that returns different objects based on input.

❓ Why interface is used?

👉 To achieve abstraction and loose coupling.

❓ Why not directly use Circle/Rectangle?

👉 To make code flexible and scalable.

❓ Why triangle area not calculated?

👉 Simplified implementation; could use Heron’s formula.

❓ What is abstraction here?

👉 Hiding implementation and showing only method structure.

🧠 FINAL ONE-LINE SUMMARY

“This program demonstrates interface-based abstraction and runtime polymorphism using Shape interface, where Circle, Rectangle, and Triangle classes implement common methods and objects are created dynamically using a factory method.”
